.TH "LEAN" "1" "Oct 2026" "lean" "lean Manual"

.SH NAME
lean - ⚡ lean — Environment Orchestrator

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlean [command] [flags]\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
lean manages environment profiles and keeps the resolved active environment in .env.

Normal profiles are root-level .env.<profile> files. .env is the current application of a profile, not a profile itself.

When a profile is applied or updated, lean snapshots the existing .env before replacing it.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Project configuration is stored in .lean/lean.toml.
User-wide configuration is stored in ~/.lean/config.toml.

Local configuration contains project settings such as the default profile, schema path, and output format. Global configuration contains user settings such as the editor and secret backend.

The old ~/.lean/lean.toml location is accepted as a legacy read-only fallback when ~/.lean/config.toml does not exist.

.SH GIT
When initialized inside a Git worktree, lean adds .lean and .env.* to .git/info/exclude while explicitly allowing .env.template and .env.example.

